--- Socket Demultiplexing (Sports-App Server 203.0.113.5) ---
  1. TCP 49.37.2.8:50001 -> 443    => Socket: TCP 203.0.113.5:443 <-> 49.37.2.8:50001 (ESTABLISHED)
  2. TCP 117.96.4.2:50000 -> 443   => Socket: TCP 203.0.113.5:443 <-> 117.96.4.2:50000 (ESTABLISHED)
  3. TCP SYN 106.51.7.7:41000->443 => Socket: TCP 203.0.113.5:443 (LISTEN) -> spawns new conn socket
  4. UDP 49.37.2.8:50000 -> 5004   => Socket: UDP 203.0.113.5:5004 (shared 2-tuple socket)
  Why: TCP demultiplexes on 4-tuple (srcIP, srcPort, dstIP, dstPort); UDP demultiplexes on 2-tuple (dstIP, dstPort).

--- Header Overhead (100-byte Score Update + 20B IPv4) ---
  UDP + IPv4 : 8 + 20 = 28 B header / 128 B total = 21.88%
  TCP + IPv4 : 20 + 20 = 40 B header / 140 B total = 28.57%

